# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: deferred-dxf-header-only-header-variables -- clautolisp writes every sysvar into a DXF header, the CADs only the DXF header variables
#+STATUS: DEFERRED
#+PRIORITY: P4
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: dxf-writer-header-not-utf8
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-25

Found closing dxf-writer-header-not-utf8 (2026-10-25). DXF-WRITE-HEADER
(clautolisp/drawing/source/dxf.lisp) emits every sysvar cell of the drawing
as a $NAME header variable. The CADs write only the documented DXF header
variables: the dxf-angles DXF of AutoCAD 2022 and BricsCAD V25 / V26 have no
$AREAUNITS, $LENGTHUNITS, $VOLUMEUNITS (BricsCAD sysvars), which clautolisp
writes -- $LENGTHUNITS with its quotes ("\"in ft mi ...\""). They also
write $DWGCODEPAGE with group code 3; clautolisp with 1 (the code
DXF-HEADER-VALUE-CODE picks for a string).

Readers skip unknown header variables, so nothing breaks today. To do: keep
the header to the DXF reference's variables, each with its documented group
code (a table, checked against the vendor files in dist/dxf-angles/ or
clautolisp/drawing/tests/fixtures/vendor-dxf/), and decide where the other
sysvars live (a clautolisp-only section, or not at all).
